* DUT -- design/netlist/bandgap_amp.spice, verbatim. in_p <- sns2
* (non-inverting), in_n <- sns1 (inverting), out -> fb -- same polarity
* design/bandgap_amp.sch's own header derives and
* sim/closed-loop-vref-pvt/ and sim/closed-loop-startup/ both use.
XMTAIL tail fb vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMP1 d1 sns2 tail vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=20u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMP2 d2 sns1 tail vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=20u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMP3 pn pn vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMP4 fb pn vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMN1 d1 d1 vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMN2 d2 d2 vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMN3 fb d1 vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
XMN4 pn d2 vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1

* DUT -- design/netlist/bandgap_startup.spice, verbatim. `sns1` and `fb`
* are shared with the core and amp DUTs above -- the nodes the assembled
* block actually connects. No separate stimulus source drives either one.
*
* FIXTURE -- Vmkfb is a 0V ammeter in series with XMKFB's drain (same
* fixture every closed-loop experiment in this tree uses), so the startup
* circuit's own contribution to the shared fb node can be measured
* directly if needed. A 0V source is a DC/AC short and does not move the
* operating point or inject anything of its own.
XRPU vdd det sub! rhigh w=1u l=1411.3u m=1 b=0
XMSENSE det sns1 vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=10u l=0.5u ng=1 m=1
Vmkfb fb fbx dc 0
XMKFB fbx det vss vss sg13_hv_nmos w=2u l=0.5u ng=1 m=1

.control
pre_osdi /home/ubuntu/share/pdk/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi/psp103.osdi
pre_osdi /home/ubuntu/share/pdk/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi/psp103_nqs.osdi
pre_osdi /home/ubuntu/share/pdk/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi/mosvar.osdi
pre_osdi /home/ubuntu/share/pdk/ihp-sg13g2/libs.tech/ngspice/osdi/r3_cmc.osdi
op
* Sanity check (mirrors sim/loop-gain-phase-margin's "op landed near its
* seed" -- see README): if .op strayed into the wrong equilibrium, fb here
* will read far from 2.55589e+00. ngspice has no ".meas op" analysis type;
* "print" is this tree's standard way to pull a DC operating-point value
* out of a .control block, parsed by run_pvt_sweep.sh from this exact
* "v(node) = value" line shape.
print v(fb)
print v(sns1)
print v(sns2)
print v(vref)
ac dec 30 1 1e9
let psrr_db = -db(v(vref))
let vref_phase_deg = cph(v(vref))*180/PI
wrdata /home/ubuntu/GitHub/sg13g2-bandgap/.loom/worktrees/issue-264/sim/closed-loop-psrr/corners/20261001-085737-e5507b2/typ_125c_3.30v.ac.txt psrr_db vref_phase_deg
.endc
.end
